<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Süleymanshah II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1204">1204</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Rukn al-Din Süleymanshah, Suleiman II of Rum, Suleymanshah II, Rukn al-Din Suleiman II</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Süleymanshah II, Rukn al-Din, was sultan of the Seljuk <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultanate-of-rum">Sultanate of Rum</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> from 1196 to 1204. He took the throne from his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaykhusraw-i">Kaykhusraw I</a>, reunited lands divided among his brothers and annexed the Saltukid principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erzurum">Erzurum</a>. His campaign against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a> ended in defeat by the army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tamar-of-georgia">Queen Tamar</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-basiani">Basiani</a> around 1202, and he died in 1204.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/suleymanshah-ii.jpg" alt="Süleymanshah II" width="320" height="317" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 1198-9 CE · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rukn_al-Din_Sulayman_bin_Qilich_Arslan._As_sultan,_AH_593-600_(AD_1197-1204)_Dated_AH_595_(AD_1198-9)_Obverse.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
